{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Behold, etc.</b> That after \"my God is the salvation of me,\" <b>I will trust</b> [means] I will dwell securely." "<b>[YH].</b> The meaning of the half-Name is in the book of Psalms (Psalms 68:5). <b>And the song of.</b> Interpreted in the Torah (Exodus 15:2)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "Resolved abbreviation וגו' as 'etc.'; the comment parses the logical sequence of the verse.", 1 "The bracketed lemma [יה] reflects the half-Name יה (YH); 'the half-Name' refers to the poetic shortened form of the divine name."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:29.948193256Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}